Connector plugin jars distributed as release assets

Tapstate loads connector plugins as separate, independently licensed artifacts;
none of them are part of this source tree or of any Tapstate binary. For
convenience, prebuilt connector jars are published as assets on the
"connectors-preview" release for the online-runtime quickstart and explicit CLI
registration without building the connector repositories first. Those jars are
shaded and carry their own drivers on an isolated class loader:

  * mysql-connector.jar bundles Oracle MySQL Connector/J 8.0, licensed under
    GPL-2.0 with the Universal FOSS Exception. That exception is what permits its
    distribution alongside Apache-2.0 licensed software.

  * mongodb-connector.jar bundles the MongoDB Java driver (Apache-2.0) and other
    Apache-2.0 and BSD licensed components.

  * mongodb-atlas-connector.jar bundles the MongoDB Java driver and other
    dependencies; the shaded jar carries their license and notice texts under
    META-INF/.

  * oracle-connector.jar bundles Oracle Database JDBC, NLS and XML artifacts
    21.5.0.0, governed by the Oracle Free Use Terms and Conditions.

  * sqlserver-connector.jar bundles Microsoft JDBC Driver for SQL Server 12.2.0,
    licensed under the MIT License.

The release carries companion copies of the Oracle Free Use Terms and the
Microsoft MIT License beside the enterprise jars; the other jars carry their
dependency notices under META-INF/. Those terms govern only the bundled drivers
and dependencies identified above; they do not alter the Apache-2.0 license of
Tapstate itself. The Oracle and SQL Server implementations are paid connector
implementations; their use remains subject to the applicable Tapdata agreement.
